blocks.en:
We hypothesise that structuring embedding space based on predictive uncertainty can reduce catastrophic boundary deviations while preserving overall segmentation accuracy. Confident same-class voxels should anchor compact clusters, whereas high-uncertainty voxels should be prevented from distorting these regions of feature space.
We therefore propose Contrastive Uncertainty Learning (CUL), a supervised contrastive uncertainty learning framework that: (1) treats predictive uncertainty as a representation level supervisory signal rather than solely a post-hoc reliability estimate or filtering mechanism;
(2) structures representation geometry by aligning low uncertainty same class voxel features while preventing ambiguous high uncertainty features from collapsing into confident clusters;
(3) demonstrates significant surface distance (SD) improvement across 6 of 8 anatomical structures ( p < 0.001 p<0.001 ), with a 22 × 22{\times} asymmetry between significantly improved and degraded hard cases; and
(4) validates each component’s contribution via two ablations: removing uncertainty guidance achieves 5/8 significant SD anatomical structures; replacing the contrastive term with a boundary loss achieves 4/8, confirming uncertainty guided selection as the decisive factor, improving transition zone, while the contrastive mechanism additionally accounts for bladder. To our knowledge, uncertainty has not been explicitly used as a contrastive structuring signal to improve segmentation robustness.

blocks.zh:
我们假设,基于预测不确定性的嵌入空间结构可以减少灾难性的边界偏差,同时保持整体分解精度. 自信的同等花瓶应锁定紧凑的星团,而高不确定性花瓶应防止扭曲这些地物空间区域。
因此,我们提议采用对照不确定性学习(CUL)这一监督的对比不确定性学习框架:(1) 将预测不确定性视为一种表现水平监督信号,而不只是一种事后可靠性估计或过滤机制;
( 二 ) 结构 表示 几何 , 将 低 的 不确定 性 特征 等同 等 voxel 特征 , 同时 防止 模糊 的 高 不确定性 特征 倒塌 成 有 信心 的 集群 ;
(3) 在8个解剖结构中的6个结构(p < 0.001 p < 0.001)中,显示显著地表距离(SD)有显著改善,在显著改善的硬壳和已退化的硬壳之间有22×22相不对称;
(4) 通过两次模拟验证每个组成部分的贡献:消除不确定性指导实现5/8个重要的自毁解剖结构;用边界损失取代对比性术语实现4/8,确认不确定性作为决定性因素的选择,改善过渡区,而对比性机制则额外说明膀胱。 据我们所知,不确定性并未被明确用作一种对比性的结构信号来提高分化强度。
